andle a double value. This is consistent with the original code but should be verified to ensure that the logic remains correct after other changes.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java--159449:160936","promptId":"#QHXM6","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":159449,"endPos":160936,"startLine":3875,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":3896,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1488}]}]},{"comment":"The TODO comments in these diffs suggest that the `NormalizeAggregate` rule might no longer be needed. This should be investigated to ensure that the optimizer still functions correctly without this rule. If it is indeed unnecessary, the rule and its associated tests should be removed or refactored.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java-76820:76893-","promptId":"#CWR77","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":76820,"endPos":76893,"startLine":1675,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":1675,"endLineOffset":77,"length":74}],"dstChanges":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java--76820:76841","promptId":"#WDENE","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":76820,"endPos":76841,"startLine":1675,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":1675,"endLineOffset":25,"length":22}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":103,"line":103,"comment_lines":["[][103]"],"review_comment":["use field.fold() since the field can be an expression such as 1 + 1 and you want to return the surrogate before the rest of the optimizer rules kick in.","Would love to just fold, but folding here is not safe unless we check if this will fold to `null`, first. That would require duplicating logic from `FoldNull`, though, which I\u0027d prefer to avoid.\r\n\r\n(Our evaluators cannot deal with null literals in general, and folding here results in the following exception when running e.g. `count(to_double(null))`:\r\n```\r\nillegal data type [null]\r\norg.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException: illegal data type [null]\r\n\tat __randomizedtesting.SeedInfo.seed([DBCF40F13A40EC92:539B7F2B94BC816A]:0)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.CsvTests.stats.Asdf(stats.csv-spec:1708)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException.illegalDataType(EsqlIllegalArgumentException.java:43)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException.illegalDataType(EsqlIllegalArgumentException.java:39)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.convert.AbstractConvertFunction.evaluator(AbstractConvertFunction.java:65)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.convert.AbstractConvertFunction.toEvaluator(AbstractConvertFunction.java:105)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.evaluator.mapper.EvaluatorMapper.fold(EvaluatorMapper.java:48)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.EsqlScalarFunction.fold(EsqlScalarFunction.java:30)\r\n```\r\n)","Consider the rare case of count(1+1) - there might be count(1+null). This can be moved to a separate issue though to not block this one.","It makes sense to add more tests to account for these cases where an expression is evaluated, esp. to `null`. I\u0027ll do that in another PR, as this one should be backported to 8.14 as soon as possible.\r\n\r\nThese cases are covered in this PR, it\u0027s just that they result in an extra eval+projection.\r\n\r\n```\r\n| STATS count(1+null)\r\n```\r\n\r\nbecomes something equivalent to\r\n\r\n```\r\n| STATS x \u003d count(*)\r\n| EVAL `count(1+null)` \u003d COALESCE(MV_COUNT(1+null), 0) * x\r\n| KEEP `count(1+null)`\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhich after folding becomes a multiplication of `count(*)` with 0. If we wanted to, we could further optimize this case to avoid the `count(*)` as well.","Opened a PR with additional tests: https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/107888"],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","id":37860,"created_at":"2024-04-22T07:12:26Z","original_position":42,"side":"RIGHT","position":42,"submitted_on_commit":"496a2448383e0316baf22f3f3605daee2061682f","diff_hunk":"@@ -87,4 +93,30 @@ public Nullability nullable() {\n     protected TypeResolution resolveType() {\n         return EsqlTypeResolutions.isExact(field(), sourceText(), DEFAULT);\n     }\n+\n+    @Override\n+    public Expression surrogate() {\n+        var s \u003d source();\n+        var field \u003d field();\n+\n+        if (field.foldable()) {\n+            if (field instanceof Literal l) {","submitted_line":103},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The logic for handling foldable fields in the `surrogate()` method seems correct but could be simplified and made more consistent. For example, the `Count` class handles the case where `field` is a `Literal` separately, while `CountDistinct` does not. Additionally, both classes should handle the normalization of `COUNT(*)`, `COUNT()`, `COUNT(\"foobar\")`, and `COUNT(1)` as `COUNT(*)`. The commented-out TODO in `#0VTRR` suggests this normalization, but it is not implemented.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java--5928:6219","promptId":"#NFBQ1","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5928,"endPos":6219,"startLine":124,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":132,"endLineOffset":5,"length":292}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java-2365:2469-2523:2540,2549:2569,2586:2775","promptId":"#73AKB","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":2365,"endPos":2469,"startLine":66,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":66,"endLineOffset":119,"length":105}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2523,"endPos":2540,"startLine":68,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":68,"endLineOffset":25,"length":18},{"pos":2549,"endPos":2569,"startLine":69,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":69,"endLineOffset":28,"length":21},{"pos":2586,"endPos":2775,"startLine":71,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":73,"endLineOffset":118,"length":190}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java--3407:4400","promptI