ral(s, StringUtils.WILDCARD, DataTypes.KEYWORD));\n+                    return null;\n+                }\n+            }\n+\n+            // COUNT(const) is equivalent to MV_COUNT(const)*COUNT(*) if const is not null; otherwise COUNT(const) \u003d\u003d 0.\n+            return new Mul(\n+                s,\n+                new Coalesce(s, new MvCount(s, field), List.of(new Literal(s, 0, DataTypes.INTEGER))),\n+                new Count(s, new Literal(s, StringUtils.WILDCARD, DataTypes.KEYWORD))","submitted_line":116},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The logic for handling foldable fields in the `surrogate()` method seems correct but could be simplified and made more consistent. For example, the `Count` class handles the case where `field` is a `Literal` separately, while `CountDistinct` does not. Additionally, both classes should handle the normalization of `COUNT(*)`, `COUNT()`, `COUNT(\"foobar\")`, and `COUNT(1)` as `COUNT(*)`. The commented-out TODO in `#0VTRR` suggests this normalization, but it is not implemented.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java--5928:6219","promptId":"#NFBQ1","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5928,"endPos":6219,"startLine":124,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":132,"endLineOffset":5,"length":292}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java-2365:2469-2523:2540,2549:2569,2586:2775","promptId":"#73AKB","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/e